# Local environment (flutter_dotenv).
#
# `flutter_app/.env` IS TRACKED, on purpose. pubspec.yaml lists `.env` under
# `flutter: assets:` so flutter_dotenv can bundle it, and Flutter fails the
# build when a declared asset is missing -- a fresh clone (and therefore CI)
# used to break `flutter analyze --fatal-infos` with `asset_does_not_exist`.
# The tracked file is a comment-only placeholder.
#
# The `!/.env` rule below just keeps this file out of the ignore list. Note
# that ignore rules have NO effect on a path git already tracks, so nothing
# here stops a real key from being committed once you type one into `.env`.
#
# Two safe ways to supply IMGBB_API_KEY, best first:
#
#   1. Do not use .env at all -- pass it at build time (see docs/IMGBB_SETUP.md):
#        flutter run --dart-define=IMGBB_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY
#
#   2. If you want it in .env, hide your local copy from git first:
#        echo 'IMGBB_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY' >> flutter_app/.env
#        git update-index --skip-worktree flutter_app/.env
#      Undo with: git update-index --no-skip-worktree flutter_app/.env
#
# Check before every commit that `git status` does not list flutter_app/.env.
!/.env
/.env.*.local

# Widget Preview related
.widget_preview/
